   "id": 1,
   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "COMEDY\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 5, CC 97 to 112\n   1 Kind of joke\n   2 What the joke is about\n   3 Pause before the punchline\n   4 Escalation\n   5 Absurdity\n   6 Deadpan to broad\n   7 Cringe\n   8 Setup and payoff\n   9 Scenes from setup to payoff\n  10 Laughs per minute\n  11 Who carries the joke\n  12 Reaction to the joke\n  13 Running gag\n  14 Callback\n  15 Rule of three\n  16 Physical comedy\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 6, CC 1 to 16\n   1 Wordplay\n   2 Misdirection\n   3 Irony\n   4 Understatement\n   5 Fish out of water\n   6 Visual gag\n   7 Subversion\n   8 Comic edit\n   9 Comic sound\n  10 suite: Comedy lens\n  11 suite: Where the laugh comes from\n  12 suite: Deadpan\n  13 suite: Slapstick\n  14 suite: Mockumentary\n  15 suite: Screwball\n  16 suite: Cringe comedy\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 6, CC 17 to 32\n   1 suite: Absurdist\n   2 suite: Dark comedy\n   3 suite: Rom-com banter\n   4 suite: Snowball disaster\n   5 suite: Pull-back reveal\n   6 suite: Smash cut contradiction\n   7 suite: Background gags\n   8 pair: When a joke's setup is planted, the payoff lands\n   9 pair: When the escalation rises, the absurdity rises\n  10 pair: When the pause before the punchline grows, laughs per minute drop but each lands harder\n  11 pair: After a big joke, cut to a reaction\n  12 pair: Two of a pattern, then the break\n  13 pair: \"I'll never\", then they do\n  14 pair: After a cringe, a pointed silence\n  15 pair: As trouble escalates, the frame widens\n  16 pair: A running gag returns, bigger\nCV-CC 4: MIDI channel 6, CC 33 to 40\n   1 pair: A joke line returns in a tender moment\n   2 pair: Something absurd, nobody reacts\n   3 pair: Misdirection pays off with a pull-back\n   4 pair: After tension, a laugh breaks it\n   5 pairs: Joke machine\n   6 pairs: Long-game comedy\n   7 pairs: Comic reversals\n   8 pairs: The camera sells the joke"
   },
